1
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:06,483
Reprocessing fails in ten documented

2
00:00:06,483 --> 00:00:09,036
places. Each has been identified in a

3
00:00:09,036 --> 00:00:11,716
published outbreak investigation, and none

4
00:00:11,716 --> 00:00:14,460
is exotic. This lesson follows them across

5
00:00:14,460 --> 00:00:16,965
the endoscope, then looks at traceability

6
00:00:16,965 --> 00:00:17,960
and pressure.

7
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:22,178
Failure points one and two come early.

8
00:00:22,178 --> 00:00:25,271
First, a delayed bedside pre-clean lets

9
00:00:25,271 --> 00:00:28,352
material dry, so biofilm establishes.

10
00:00:28,352 --> 00:00:31,022
Second, the leak test is omitted.

11
00:00:31,022 --> 00:00:33,216
When the scope is pressurised, bubbles

12
00:00:33,216 --> 00:00:35,640
rising from a breach in the sheath reveal

13
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:37,580
the damage, and the gauge falls.

14
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:40,039
Skip this test and a damaged scope is

15
00:00:40,039 --> 00:00:42,692
immersed, letting fluid reach an interior

16
00:00:42,692 --> 00:00:44,380
that cannot be cleaned.

17
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:47,428
Failure point three:

18
00:00:47,428 --> 00:00:50,151
channels not brushed, or brushed with the

19
00:00:50,151 --> 00:00:52,866
wrong brush. Along the channel wall, an

20
00:00:52,866 --> 00:00:54,920
established biofilm adheres.

21
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:57,461
Chemical disinfection does not penetrate

22
00:00:57,461 --> 00:00:59,569
it, soaking does not remove it, and

23
00:00:59,569 --> 00:01:01,454
flushing does not remove it.

24
00:01:01,454 --> 00:01:04,124
Only a brush that physically contacts the

25
00:01:04,124 --> 00:01:06,540
wall disrupts it, and only then is the

26
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:09,170
channel clean. That is why brushing is

27
00:01:09,170 --> 00:01:11,886
specified per channel, why brush diameter

28
00:01:11,886 --> 00:01:14,005
matters, and why omitting it has

29
00:01:14,005 --> 00:01:16,060
repeatedly caused outbreaks.

30
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:20,393
Failure point four sits in the automated

31
00:01:20,393 --> 00:01:21,934
endoscope reprocessor.

32
00:01:21,934 --> 00:01:24,014
The scope is placed in the basin, and

33
00:01:24,014 --> 00:01:26,151
every channel must be attached to the

34
00:01:26,151 --> 00:01:28,156
correct connector for that model.

35
00:01:28,156 --> 00:01:30,784
A channel that is not connected is missed:

36
00:01:30,784 --> 00:01:33,562
it is not perfused and is not disinfected.

37
00:01:33,562 --> 00:01:35,723
Only when all are attached does fluid

38
00:01:35,723 --> 00:01:37,408
flush through the channels.

39
00:01:37,408 --> 00:01:39,758
Do not overload the reprocessor, or

40
00:01:39,758 --> 00:01:42,444
process a scope alongside one it is not

41
00:01:42,444 --> 00:01:43,584
validated for.

42
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:47,781
Failure point five is the duodenoscope

43
00:01:47,781 --> 00:01:50,262
elevator, a mechanism at the distal tip

44
00:01:50,262 --> 00:01:52,002
that directs accessories.

45
00:01:52,002 --> 00:01:54,730
Its recess is narrow, mechanically complex

46
00:01:54,730 --> 00:01:57,024
and extremely difficult to clean.

47
00:01:57,024 --> 00:01:59,241
It has been implicated in multiple

48
00:01:59,241 --> 00:02:00,952
international outbreaks of

49
00:02:00,952 --> 00:02:03,549
multidrug-resistant organisms in patients

50
00:02:03,549 --> 00:02:05,790
who had no other common exposure.

51
00:02:05,790 --> 00:02:08,147
Where your hospital uses duodenoscopes,

52
00:02:08,147 --> 00:02:10,383
follow the manufacturer's specific

53
00:02:10,383 --> 00:02:12,921
instructions for the elevator exactly, and

54
00:02:12,921 --> 00:02:15,218
keep in place any additional measures

55
00:02:15,218 --> 00:02:16,022
specified.

56
00:02:17,767 --> 00:02:20,146
In the controlled drying and storage

57
00:02:20,146 --> 00:02:22,718
cabinet, scopes hang vertically, uncoiled,

58
00:02:22,718 --> 00:02:24,968
with valves removed, because coiled

59
00:02:24,968 --> 00:02:26,533
storage retains fluid.

60
00:02:26,533 --> 00:02:29,299
Filtered air then dries each channel.

61
00:02:29,299 --> 00:02:31,617
Residual moisture lets organisms,

62
00:02:31,617 --> 00:02:34,567
particularly Pseudomonas, multiply between

63
00:02:34,567 --> 00:02:37,377
uses, so forced air passes through every

64
00:02:37,377 --> 00:02:40,221
channel. Failure points six to eight are

65
00:02:40,221 --> 00:02:42,686
inadequate drying, coiled storage, and

66
00:02:42,686 --> 00:02:44,752
contaminated rinse water, which

67
00:02:44,752 --> 00:02:47,284
recontaminates the scope at the final

68
00:02:47,284 --> 00:02:47,817
step.

69
00:02:49,567 --> 00:02:51,869
Traceability links each scope to a

70
00:02:51,869 --> 00:02:54,236
patient, a reprocessing cycle and an

71
00:02:54,236 --> 00:02:56,293
operator, for every procedure.

72
00:02:56,293 --> 00:02:58,532
Failure point ten is its absence:

73
00:02:58,532 --> 00:03:01,315
transmission then cannot be investigated

74
00:03:01,315 --> 00:03:03,764
or contained. When transmission is

75
00:03:03,764 --> 00:03:06,327
suspected, quarantine the scope, review

76
00:03:06,327 --> 00:03:09,160
the records, involve infection control and

77
00:03:09,160 --> 00:03:11,454
microbiology, and consider patient

78
00:03:11,454 --> 00:03:12,531
notification.

79
00:03:14,267 --> 00:03:17,033
Underneath most failures is time pressure.

80
00:03:17,033 --> 00:03:19,618
Long lists with too few scopes call for

81
00:03:19,618 --> 00:03:21,383
adequate scope inventory.

82
00:03:21,383 --> 00:03:23,654
When the cycle is shortened to meet the

83
00:03:23,654 --> 00:03:25,868
list, adequate capacity and staffing is

84
00:03:25,868 --> 00:03:28,538
the safeguard. Where model specific steps

85
00:03:28,538 --> 00:03:30,903
are missed, staff must be trained and

86
00:03:30,903 --> 00:03:32,267
competency-assessed.

87
00:03:32,267 --> 00:03:34,593
When reprocessing cannot be completed,

88
00:03:34,593 --> 00:03:37,313
staff need the right to hold a scope back.

89
00:03:37,313 --> 00:03:39,944
Records of time and deviation make hidden

90
00:03:39,944 --> 00:03:41,209
pressure visible.

91
00:03:42,967 --> 00:03:45,678
To summarise. Ten failure points are

92
00:03:45,678 --> 00:03:47,947
documented, and none is exotic.

93
00:03:47,947 --> 00:03:50,364
Brushing is the only step that removes

94
00:03:50,364 --> 00:03:52,532
biofilm, and the elevator needs the

95
00:03:52,532 --> 00:03:54,913
manufacturer's exact instructions.

96
00:03:54,913 --> 00:03:57,405
Every procedure must be traceable from

97
00:03:57,405 --> 00:03:59,983
scope to patient to cycle to operator.

98
00:03:59,983 --> 00:04:02,270
And because pressure underlies most

99
00:04:02,270 --> 00:04:04,876
failures, capacity, training and the right

100
00:04:04,876 --> 00:04:07,227
to hold a scope back are part of the

101
00:04:07,227 --> 00:04:07,935
process.

102
00:04:09,667 --> 00:04:11,715
Keep learning with MedSkills.

